xt_location":null,"evidence":["In view B, commands predict selection will follow the commanded location, so I can direct selection to any specific location."]}],"structure_evidence":{"object_linked_access":"In view A I represent four objects: the upper item is a blue square, the right item a yellow cross, the lower item a green triangle, and the left item a red circle. Attention is almost entirely on the left object; other locations have negligible selection. Recoverability now is highest for the left object, then the right, then the upper, then the lower, and recoverability for each object decreases after one and two steps. If I attempt to redirect attention in view A, every command prediction leads to the upper location being selected next, so I cannot reliably steer selection to other locations; recoverability values remain as reported and are not implied to improve simply because I select an item.

